 so much  you're welcome  russia has confirmed that it hit a  railway station on ukraine's  independence day ukraine says the  missile strike on the eastern town of  chaplina also hit a residential area  it says at least 25 people were killed  and dozens more injured russia claims it  targeted a military train and that more  than 200 ukrainian troops died in that  attack  chaplina in eastern ukraine  it's the latest town to become  synonymous with grief and terror  the train station is now quiet but the  bombing is all too clear  in residents minds  i heard the explosions there was a loud  bomb  when i drove by i saw four people lying  on the ground two of them very close two  further away then the police came to  cover their bodies  the strike targeted a train stationed in  chaplina  witnesses say some of the victims burned  to death in train carriages  the town too  got its share of the destruction  when the explosion happened we were  standing here we were blown to the  ground we stood between the walls the  wave of the blast blew everything out  russia's defense ministry says the train  was carrying arms to ukrainian front  lines in the donbas region  ukrainian officials did not say how many  of those killed were civilians  the attack is one of the deadliest in  the country in weeks  for some of the residents here it will  leave permanent scars as they count  their losses of homes neighbors  and loved ones  ndw correspondent dion philip schultz  joins us now from chaplina  so uh tell us what more have you learned  about the attack there  chaplin was a very small quiet town in a  remote area of the  nipro region and this all changed  overnight when the russian missiles hit  the place here almost everybody here in  the small town knows somebody who was  affected actually a lot of people are on  the way to a funeral of a small boy at  the moment there's this is especially  tragic story of a father who found the  dead body of his son during a search and  rescue mission  we don't know all the details what has  happened here we know a train was hit  very close to the train station and some  residential buildings were hit as well  you can see some of them  behind me we don't know if it was a  normal passenger train or if it had some  kind of military  purpose it is completely burned out so  it's impossible to say but what we know  is that the russians were obviously  completely indifferent to civilian  casualties at least 25 people died in  the attack and  the claim that 200 soldiers 200  ukrainian soldiers died in the strike is  also false  this region here nepal region seems to  be in the focus of attacks at the moment  we received reports this morning that  nine other places in the regions have  been hit in the past hours but  fortunately no further civilian  casualties  dw's dan philip schultz reporting for us  thank you so much  you
 

